viv: Go example? show a compact recv loop that sets cursor from a metadata field and retries on transient errors. keep it small.

emily: Go (compact):
```go
ctx := context.Background()
var cursor string = ""
for attempt := 0; attempt < 3; attempt++ {
    stream, err := client.GenerateStream(ctx, &GenerateOptions{Prompt: prompt, Cursor: cursor})
    if err != nil {
        time.Sleep(time.Duration(100*(1<<attempt)) * time.Millisecond)
        continue
    }
    for {
        msg, err := stream.Recv()
        if err == io.EOF { break }
        if err != nil { /* treat as transient and break to retry */ break }
        fmt.Print(msg.Text)
        if msg.Cursor != "" { cursor = msg.Cursor }
    }
    break
}
```

sanjay: small style nit: in Go snippet prefer 'curs' local var name to avoid shadowing package-level names; i'll leave an inline nit on the PR. otherwise lgtm.

